<p>Specifications as published by Hytrol distributors Cisco-Eagle (199-CRR, 26-CRR) and ACG Conveyors (36-CRRH). Other manufacturers rate their models differently, so compare per-foot and per-roller ratings at your support spacing. Cost rises with roller diameter and wall, chain size, frame weight and support count, length, number of drives or zones, and transfers and controls. See the <a href="/resources/conveyor-cost-guide/">cost guide</a> for cost factors.</p>
<h2 id="apps-heading">CDLR Conveyor Applications</h2>
<p><strong>Pallet conveyor systems:</strong> CDLR is the default drive technology for <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">pallet conveyor systems</a>. Loaded pallets move between palletizers, stretch wrappers, labelers, and shipping docks on CDLR conveyors. Right-angle chain <a href="/conveyor-types/transfer-conveyors/">transfers</a> route pallets to multiple shipping lanes.</p>
<figure class="photo"><img src="/img/photos/cdlr-hytrol-pallet-merge.webp" width="1000" height="667" alt="Overhead view of pallets of cartons and shrink-wrapped bottles on blue roller conveyor lines, with a curve joining a side line to the main line." loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Loaded pallets on Hytrol chain driven live roller conveyor, with a curve feeding a side line into the main line. <span class="photo-credit">Photo: <a href="https://hytrol.com/products/pallet-handling/chain-roller-conveyor/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hytrol</a></span></figcaption></figure>
<p><strong>Drum and barrel handling:</strong> Steel drums and barrels ride on CDLR rollers. The positive chain drive avoids the slip that friction-driven rollers can have with smooth drum bottoms. Chemical, petroleum, and <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/">food processing</a> facilities use CDLR for drum transport.</p>
<p><strong>Heavy case transport:</strong> Heavy cases and totes, such as automotive parts, appliance components, and industrial goods, use CDLR when they exceed the rating of lighter conveyors. Positive drive keeps speed steady as load changes.</p>
<p><strong>Between palletizer and stretch wrapper:</strong> The section between the palletizer discharge and the stretch wrapper infeed is a key CDLR application in <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/">packaging lines</a>. Full pallets must transfer reliably and stop in position for the wrapper's turntable or rotary ring. CDLR provides the torque and positive drive this application needs.</p>
<p><strong>With <a href="/conveyor-types/vertical-reciprocating/">vertical reciprocating conveyors</a>:</strong> CDLR sections feed loaded pallets onto VRC platforms for multi-level transport. Positive drive helps load and unload the VRC reliably, even with heavy or off-center pallet loads.</p>
<h2 id="maintenance-heading">CDLR Maintenance</h2>
<p>CDLR conveyors need more routine maintenance than <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR conveyors</a> but handle loads that MDR cannot. Hytrol's installation and maintenance manuals for its CRR and CREZD models set out these items:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Chain lubrication:</strong> Lubricate the drive chain every 2,080 hours of operation or every 6 months, whichever comes first, in normal environments. Lubricate more often in damp, dusty, high-speed, or high-temperature service, and set a custom interval by inspecting the chain. Use food-grade (H1) lubricant in <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/">food and beverage</a> environments.</li>
<li><strong>Chain stretch and sprocket wear:</strong> Hytrol lists lack of lubrication as a cause of chain stretch, which creates poor chain-to-sprocket mesh and excessive sprocket wear. Replace stretched chain and worn sprockets at the chain maker's wear limits.</li>
<li><strong>Chain tension:</strong> Check tension at regular intervals. Loose chains can skip sprocket teeth. Over-tight chains accelerate bearing and sprocket wear.</li>
<li><strong>Bearings and set screws:</strong> Hytrol calls for checking set screws after the first 24 hours of operation. Investigate popping or grinding bearing noise, which Hytrol links to defective bearings or loose set screws.</li>
<li><strong>Motor and reducer:</strong> Service per the manufacturer schedule. Overheating can point to an overloaded conveyor or low voltage.</li>
</ul>
