<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What does CDLR stand for?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>CDLR stands for Chain Driven Live Roller. Roller chain and sprockets positively drive all rollers with no slip. CDLR is the standard for <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">pallet conveying</a> and heavy unit loads.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is the weight capacity of a CDLR conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Capacity is rated per linear foot and depends on roller size, chain, frame, and support spacing. Hytrol examples: 199-CRR at 150 lbs per foot, 26-CRR at 300 lbs per foot on 10-foot supports or 1,000 lbs per foot on 5-foot supports, and 36-CRRH at 2,000 lbs per foot on 5-foot supports. Check both the per-foot rating and the load on each roller for your heaviest pallet.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">When should I use CDLR instead of MDR?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Use CDLR when loads exceed the rating of MDR or belt-driven roller, you need positive drive with no slip, or product bottoms slip on friction-driven rollers. Use <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR</a> for lighter loads needing simple zone control. Zoned CDLR also provides zero-pressure <a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">accumulation</a> with a gearmotor per zone.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What maintenance does CDLR require?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Chain lubrication every 2,080 hours or 6 months, whichever comes first, in normal environments per Hytrol's manuals, and more often in harsh service. Lack of lubrication causes chain stretch and sprocket wear. Also check chain tension, sprockets, bearings, and set screws, and service the motor and reducer per the manufacturer schedule.</p>

</div>
</div>
